      "title": "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "537329c9-554d-5577-889d-07ac1b1e28d5",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/17/1745c1d24e42b7335d18f7462d0e2ecaf4ed53c8eac747ec62fad3ce004dc8ee.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "dccf2a8c-9052-533a-ae00-d13bfae461fb",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "3ade987a-39df-5006-be15-1e4c75ceca0b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{2(x-2)}{y-2}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "b1392acf-f660-5e14-8239-7655fe393caa",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{y-2}{4(x-2)}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "9f6cae18-5de5-56a5-8196-73feb308ffc1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{4(x-2)}{y-2}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "2c11a394-f711-5fd4-9d59-4d560ae73ccf",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{x-2}{4(y-2)}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "16e9d237-1913-5b80-82da-aace2406dbc7",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{4(x-2)}{y-2}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "16e9d237-1913-5b80-82da-aace2406dbc7"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since our ellipse is centered at $(2,2)$ and has semiaxes $1$ and $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\\,\u27f9\\,(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x-2)^{2}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x-2)^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}\\right) & =0 \\\\ 2(x-2)+\\frac{2(y-2)}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y-2}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x-2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4(x-2)}{y-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
    "generation": {
