    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e90d3a9b-8614-5230-b8c5-4d4ebc80dd69",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/fa/facae1d5ef6f154069458b2e23d286c5b6a1236603214692ac978e5dc91f3475.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "725f109c-a6fe-5db5-bf32-10918d6df266",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "a4ca343e-091d-5018-ae61-15b74971cba4",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{4(x-2)}{5(y+3)}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "052899c5-b9c8-57eb-9f10-fc35d682328d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{16(x-2)}{25(y+3)}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "554cdb50-faa9-551f-98ac-36375d50b37f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{25(y+3)}{16(x-2)}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "f0944194-081d-5b1e-a2d3-927fbc1e36ee",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{16(x-2)}{25(y+3)}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "f4769407-63ce-55de-a206-f7ab1104c2e4",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{25(x-2)}{16(y+3)}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "f0944194-081d-5b1e-a2d3-927fbc1e36ee"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since our ellipse is centered at $(2,-3)$ and has semiaxes $5$ and $4,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{{4}^{2}}=1\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{25}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16}\\right) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(x-2)}{25}+\\frac{2(y+3)}{16}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y+3}{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2(x-2)}{25} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{16(x-2)}{25(y+3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
