      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since our ellipse is centered at $(-1,1)$ and has semiaxes $5$ and $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{25}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4}\\right) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(x+1)}{25}+\\frac{2(y-1)}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y-1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2(x+1)}{25} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4(x+1)}{25(y-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
